-- @@ L9-28 verbatim
/-!
# Relative Theorem A on `U × ℙ¹`

Let `𝒢` be a coherent sheaf on `U × ℙ¹ ⊆ P^an` and `K ⊆ U` a closed box. We show that there are
an open box `B₁ ⊇ K` and `n₀` such that for `n ≥ n₀` the sections of `𝒢(n)` over `B₁ × ℙ¹`
generate `𝒢(n)` near every point of `B₁ × ℙ¹`
(`ComplexAnalytic.relProjectiveLine.exists_generates_twistMod`): the map `π^* π_* 𝒢(n) → 𝒢(n)`
is surjective over `B₁`.

Let `x₀` be a point of the chart `0` with fibre coordinate `c`, `‖c‖ ≤ 1`. We write `𝒢` as a
quotient of the vector bundle `E` of `ComplexAnalytic.relProjectiveLine.BundleData`, generated by
`s` near the chart box at `0`, and split `sⱼ / (z - c)` on an annulus `{4/3 < ‖z‖ < 3}`
avoiding `c` (`ComplexAnalytic.relProjectiveLine.BundleData.exists_split`). Multiplying by the
section `z - c` of `𝒪(1)` gives sections `Σⱼ` of `𝒢(n)` over `B₁ × ℙ¹` with `Σⱼ = sⱼ - (z - c) Φⱼ`
near `x₀`, where `Φⱼ` is an explicit combination of the `s`. The matrix expressing the `Σⱼ` in
terms of the `sⱼ` is the identity at `x₀`, hence invertible near `x₀`, so the `Σⱼ` generate `𝒢(n)`
near `x₀` (`ComplexAnalytic.relProjectiveLine.exists_generates_of_matrix`). Points of the chart
`1` are treated in the same way with the generators `t`, the section `w - c` and the annulus
`{1/3 < ‖z‖ < 3/4}`.
-/


